5. IMPORTANT NEW RESOURCE CONTRACT

Claude Code's latest prepared contract established several concepts that must be preserved.

Identity decomposition

Do not fold all identity into one hash.

Conceptually distinguish:

address_id
derivation_id
value_id
environment_id
build_id
content_id
execution_id
view/session_id

The intended semantics are roughly:

address_id
    = H(normalized address)

derivation_id
    = H(sequence of (operation, operation version, parameters))

value_id
    = H(canonical value of its kind)

environment_id
    = H(observed capabilities)

build_id
    = H(source value + compiler/version + target + config + dependencies)

content_id
    = H(bytes)

execution_id
    = H(derivation + environment + implementation versions + occurrence)

A session/view identifier is ephemeral.

Semantic equivalence does NOT receive a cryptographic identity merely because two things appear equivalent.

Semantic equivalence remains a recorded claim supported by evidence.

There was also a known defect in the implementation where "deterministic_sha256" mixed address and value; that should be treated as a concrete implementation correction, not a theoretical detail.

