6. ONE UNIVERSE, THREE REGIMES

The research direction now explicitly distinguishes:

Values

Global by construction when their address/value semantics make them identical.

If two participants resolve the same canonical value:

same address
+
same value

there is nothing inherently requiring synchronization.

Records

Executions, observations, proposals, terms, etc.

These become shared/global only when published through an authoritative shared log/resource such as Relay/ACSP/PURL.

Effects

Actual externally consequential effects.

These remain scoped until authority/effect rules exist and are experimentally tested.

This gives:

VALUES
    global by construction

RECORDS
    globally observable when published

EFFECTS
    scoped until authorized

Do not introduce unnecessary synchronization merely because multiple agents observe the same computational universe.

